From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/25] apklayer: dlsym-rtld-next-host-fallback

dlsym(RTLD_NEXT, name) falls back to the host's symbol when no later bionic library has it: Gecko's mozglue interposes putenv/setenv and crashes ("interposition failed") when RTLD_NEXT finds nothing, because the real libc is the host's glibc here.

apklayer patch: step 12 of the former scripts/patch-bionic-translation.sh (see docs/PATCHES.md), patch 0017 of patches/bionic_translation.
---
 linker/dlfcn.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/linker/dlfcn.c b/linker/dlfcn.c
index bdbdef0..01beeb1 100644
--- a/linker/dlfcn.c
+++ b/linker/dlfcn.c
@@ -174,6 +174,13 @@ void *bionic_dlsym(void *handle, const char *symbol)
 		if (si && si->next) {
 			sym = apkenv_lookup(symbol, &found, si->next);
 		}
+		if (!sym) { /* apklayer patch: see scripts/patch-bionic-translation.sh step 12 */
+			void *host = dlsym(RTLD_DEFAULT, symbol);
+			if (host) {
+				pthread_mutex_unlock(&apkenv_dl_lock);
+				return wrapper_create(symbol, host);
+			}
+		}
 	} else if (is_this_our_handle) {
 		found = (soinfo *)handle;
 		sym = apkenv_lookup_in_library(&found, symbol);
